rows=[
('raw::323',1003,4,'theory','I_force_motion;III_ideal_gas;VII_magnetic_field','Given two magnetic-moment orientations, classical dipole-gradient force, long-wire magnetic fields, beam kinematics and uncertainty','The two allowed atom moments +/-mu along x are explicitly assumed, not to be derived using spin operators. C3 explicitly supplies the air-gap field assumption and exempts its derivation. Remaining A-H is equipartition (given), classical magnetic force/fields, differentiating geometry, trajectories and error propagation.',1,True),
('raw::324',1010,4,'theory','I_force_motion;II_oscillations_waves','Rotating-hoop bead force balance, supplied friction model, equilibrium stability, potential Taylor expansion and given magnetic-transition analogy','The full A-C parent supplies the free-body diagram, restriction to the shown forces, polar acceleration, friction rule, Taylor expansions and small-oscillation formula. Magnetic Landau free energy and magnetization law are explicitly supplied only for comparison with a mechanically derived bifurcation. No critical-fluctuation, microscopic magnetism or advanced thermodynamic prerequisite is required.',0,True),
('raw::325',1016,4,'theory','VI_electric_field;II_oscillations_waves;IX_em_oscillations_waves;X_wave_optics','Uniform-cloud electrostatic restoring force, driven oscillator, dimensionally specified radiation model, intensity-loss ODE and horizon geometry','The molecule is explicitly a rigid uniform spherical charge cloud. Gauss/Coulomb force and the driven oscillator close A. B lists every radiation variable and supplies the dimensionless coefficient, so dimensional analysis gives dipole power without deriving a specialized radiation law. Intensity/power loss relations are given; aerosol cross section dependence and coefficient supplied. Geometry and elementary attenuation close D-G.',0,True),
('raw::326',1022,5,'experimental','VII_magnetic_field;VIII_induction;I_force_motion','Given dipole field, magnetometer location/calibration, graph-based falling-magnet speed and hidden pipe lengths','The full A-B simulation experiment supplies both bar-magnet field formulas, point-dipole approximation and m*y-double-dot=m*g-k*y-dot. Hall-effect microscopic transport and eddy-current field derivation are not requested. Central work locates a sensor, fits the dipole moment, inverts magnetic-field data and infers velocities/section lengths. Source-linked simulator archive preserved with provenance and limited runtime validation.',0,False),
('raw::327',1026,4,'experimental','I_force_motion;II_oscillations_waves','Classical sound Doppler effect with propagation delay, circular-plus-linear source kinematics, triangulation and experimental parameter fitting','The complete A1-A7 task is a single sound-simulation experiment with speed of sound and subsonic source specified. Ordinary sound Doppler and retarded travel-time geometry close all parameter inference. Official solution uses stationary detectors for the meaningful inference, remaining available despite the preserved simulator moving-detector input bug. No relativity or specialist inverse-wave theory required.',1,True)]
